d with an identical, public path.toNamespacedPath() method.\\n\\n[characters 22427-22553]\\nREPLServer.prototype.memory() is only necessary for the internal mechanics of the REPLServer itself. Do not use this function.\\n\\n[characters 23532-23731]\\nThe v8/* modules do not have any exports, and if not imported in a specific order would in fact throw errors. As such there are virtually no legitimate use cases for importing them through require().\\n\\n[characters 24446-24677]\\nImporting assert directly was not recommended as the exposed functions use loose equality checks. The deprecation was revoked because use of the node:assert module is not discouraged, and the deprecation caused developer confusion.\\n\\n[characters 25569-25582]\\nType: Runtime\\n\\n[characters 25854-25867]\\nType: Runtime\\n\\n[characters 26596-26609]\\nType: Runtime\\n\\n[characters 28615-28928]\\nWhen assigning a non-string property to process.env, the assigned value is implicitly converted to a string. This behavior is deprecated if the assigned value is not a string, boolean, or number. In the future, such assignment might result in a thrown error. Please convert the property to a string before assigni\",\"truncated\":true,\"query\":\"DEP0190 not escaped space-separated Runtime 24.0.0\",\"excerpts\":[{\"charStart\":266,\"charEnd\":356,\"text\":\"Documentation-only\\nApplication (non-node_modules code only)\\nRuntime (all code)\\nEnd-of-Life\"},{\"charStart\":358,\"charEnd\":842,\"text\":\"A Documentation-only deprecation is one that is expressed only within the Node.js API docs. These generate no side-effects while running Node.js. Some Documentation-only deprecations trigger a runtime warning when launched with --pending-deprecation flag (or its alternative, NODE_PENDING_DEPRECATION=1 environment variable), similarly to Runtime deprecations below. Documentation-only deprecations that support that flag are explicitly labeled as such in the list of Deprecated APIs.\"},{\"charStart\":844,\"